+\paragraph{Absolute Galois restriction and arithmetic witnesses (Block 26).}
+Fix a cyclotomic number field $L=\Q(\zeta_n)$ with $n>0$ and an embedding
+$j:L\hookrightarrow\overline{\Q}$. The new restriction map
+\[
+ q_L:G_{\Q}\longrightarrow\operatorname{Gal}(L/\Q),\qquad
+ j(q_L(\gamma)x)=\gamma(j(x)),
+\]
+is an actual continuous surjective homomorphism with open kernel. Surjectivity
+is derived by extending automorphisms to the algebraic closure. Pullback along
+a surjective homomorphism preserves and reflects equivariant linear
+isomorphisms, invariant subspaces, and irreducibility. These assertions keep
+the underlying linear maps and submodules and do not assume a finite acting
+group. In particular, the equivalence relation for systems is preserved and
+reflected componentwise.
+
+The arithmetic witnesses use the integral closure
+$\mathcal A$ of $\mathbb Z$ in $\overline{\Q}$. For each rational prime $p$,
+Lean constructs a maximal ideal $\mathfrak Q$ of $\mathcal A$ above $(p)$ and
+an actual element $\gamma_p\in G_{\Q}$ such that
+\[
+ \gamma_p\in\operatorname{Stab}_{G_{\Q}}(\mathfrak Q),\qquad
+ \overline{\gamma_p(a)}=\overline a^{\,p}
+ \quad(a\in\mathcal A).
+\]
+The existence argument applies Mathlib's proved profinite stabilizer-surjectivity
+theorem to this actual invariant ring. The residue $p$-power map is proved
+bijective by taking $p$-th roots in $\overline{\Q}$ and showing that they
+remain integral when their $p$-th powers are integral. This constructs an
+arithmetic Frobenius witness in the prime-ideal decomposition group; it does
+not assert that an arbitrary global lift belongs to that group.
+
+When $p\nmid n$, the comparison with the finite cyclotomic sample is proved:
+\[
+ q_L(\gamma_p)=\sigma_p,
+ \qquad \sigma_p(\zeta_n)=\zeta_n^p.
+\]
+Reduction distinguishes $n$-th roots of unity at such a prime. Indeed, if
+$x^n=y^n=1$ and their reductions agree, the factorization of $x^n-y^n$ gives
+\[
+ (x-y)\sum_{i=0}^{n-1}x^i y^{n-1-i}=0.
+\]
+The second factor reduces to $n\overline y^{\,n-1}\ne0$, so the domain
+property gives $x=y$. This proves both Frobenius recognition on the
+cyclotomic generator and triviality of its inertia action. Consequently,
+every representation pulled back through $q_L$ is unramified there.
+
+The valuation formulation is checked separately. For any valuation subring
+$A\subset\overline{\Q}$ with residue characteristic $p\nmid n$, its actual
+residue-action kernel fixes every $n$-th root of unity. A supplied element of
+its decomposition subgroup with $p$-power residue action restricts to
+$\sigma_p$. These statements use Mathlib's valuation inertia and decomposition
+subgroups. No identification of the valuation and integral-closure prime
+models is assumed in the formal comparison.
+
+For a compatible family $\rho_{i,\lambda}$ of representations of the fixed
+finite group, set $V_{i,\lambda}=\rho_{i,\lambda}\circ q_L$. Suppose the
+actual absolute-Galois members are irreducible and the systems are pairwise
+componentwise nonisomorphic. The finite prime separator now yields distinct
+permitted rational primes $p_j$, actual prime ideals $\mathfrak Q_j$ and
+arithmetic Frobenius witnesses $\gamma_j$ as above, outside any prescribed
+finite set, such that the common algebraic trace matrix has nonzero
+determinant. Every coefficient embedding preserves this nonvanishing, and
+\[
+ \iota_\lambda(t_i(p_j))=
+ \operatorname{tr}(V_{i,\lambda}(\gamma_j))
+\]
+whenever $p_j$ is good for that coefficient member. The operator and trace
+values agree for every global lift with the same cyclotomic restriction.
+Neither Frobenius-witness existence nor quotient coverage is a supplied
+hypothesis in this restricted arithmetic theorem. The common cyclotomic
+factorization and the compatible trace data remain explicit hypotheses.
+
+This completes the passage to actual absolute-Galois Frobenius witnesses for
+the fixed cyclotomic class. It does not establish prime coverage for arbitrary
+finite Galois extensions. Claim 9.1 therefore remains partial, and the
+source ledger remains seventeen checked and three partial.
+
+The boundaries are formalized as well. Pullback along a nonsurjective
+homomorphism can make inequivalent irreducible representations isomorphic.
+Samples can cover one quotient while missing an open quotient of the full
+group. Finally, in $\mathbb Z_2$, the distinct square roots $1$ and $-1$ have
+the same residue, so the condition that the root order be a unit cannot be
+discarded.
 
